course: dictionary
lesson: 11123
title: Wholemeal: the whole grain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wholemeal is a word you will see on bread packets, in recipes and in food lessons. It can describe something, as in «wholemeal bread», or name the flour itself, as in «wholemeal flour». Read the words around it to find its meaning. «Whole grains such as oats and wholemeal bread give energy that lasts.» Here wholemeal bread is a kind of bread that gives energy, so it is a food, not a colour.
explain: «White flour is made from the inside of the grain, while wholemeal flour uses the whole grain, so it has more fibre.» The word while shows a difference. White flour uses only the inside of the grain. Wholemeal uses all of it, so the words whole and wholemeal fit together. The clue is in the word itself.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you think wholemeal means white, try «white bread gives energy that lasts». The sentence still works, but the clue about the whole grain no longer fits, so your meaning is wrong. Always check the clues against your idea.
fact: Wholemeal flour is made from the whole grain of wheat, including the brown outer part called the bran.
fact: Wholemeal bread, pasta and biscuits are brown and full of fibre.
fact: «Wholemeal» can be an adjective, as in «wholemeal toast», or a noun for the flour, as in «wholemeal flour».
fact: Wholemeal foods have more fibre, which helps digestion and keeps you full.
fact: In America and Canada people usually say «whole wheat» instead of wholemeal.
exercise: «White flour is made from the inside of the grain, while wholemeal flour uses the whole grain.» What is wholemeal flour made from? | *The whole grain, including the brown outer part | Only the white inside of the grain | Sugar and water | Corn only
exercise: «White flour is made from the inside of the grain, while wholemeal flour uses the whole grain, so it has more fibre.» Which flour has more fibre? | Cake flour | *Wholemeal flour | Both have exactly none | White flour
exercise: «Whole grains such as oats and wholemeal bread give energy that lasts.» Find and copy the word that names the brown outer part of the grain. | wheat | flour | fibre | *bran
test: An American cook writes «whole wheat» on a recipe. What does an English cook call the same thing? | wheat-free | brown sugar | *wholemeal | plain white
test: Wholemeal toast is healthier because it has more fibre. What does fibre help with? | *Digestion, and keeping you full | Making you sleepy | Making bread white | Growing taller
exam: Mum says, «Grab a wholemeal sandwich for lunch.» What is the sandwich made from? | Chocolate biscuits | Only white bread | Crisps | *Bread made with flour from the whole grain
